{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1208548-so-is-armor-in-mage-an-auto-soak-or-dice","id":1208548,"title":"So is armor in Mage an auto-soak or dice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-18T13:28:09-07:00","id":1208548,"title":"So is armor in Mage an auto-soak or dice?","content":"The language in some of Mage seems to imply that armor is an auto-soak rather than dice. Is this true? I'm more used to vampire, where the language is unambiguous that it's dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T13:42:30-07:00","id":1208557,"title":"","content":"I tend to run armour as extra soak dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T13:46:20-07:00","id":1208559,"title":"","content":"Dice, page 416 M20. &quot;In game terms, armor adds dice to a character\u2019s soak roll and allows a human being to soak lethal damage as well as certain types of aggravated damage \u2013 a vampire\u2019s fangs, most likely, but not fire, or Life Sphere magick.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:01:45-07:00","id":1208566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1208548-so-is-armor-in-mage-an-auto-soak-or-dice?p=1208559#post1208559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dice, page 416 M20. &quot;In game terms, armor adds dice to a character\u2019s soak roll and allows a human being to soak lethal damage as well as certain types of aggravated damage \u2013 a vampire\u2019s fangs, most likely, but not fire, or Life Sphere magick.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage has a weird hard-on for Fire. The RAW for fire damage is something I don't understand.<br /> <br /> Fire hurting Vampires really badly makes sense. They're supernaturally cursed to be vulnerable to it.<br /> <br /> But normal fires (not the super-hot ones which evaporate the liquid under your skin and kill you in seconds) would realistically inflict moderate amounts of lethal and bashing damage to non-vampires. There's no real reason that Life should heal burns from boiling water more easily than burns from a housefire. Fire should only inflict Aggravated if &quot;enhanced&quot; to do so with Quintessence, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:07:02-07:00","id":1208569,"title":"","content":"Frankly I'm iffy about fire even in the case of vampires. Many versions of vampires aren't &quot;vulnerable&quot; to fire per se. They just aren't particularly invulnerable to it, and the fact that it eventually destroys something utterly instead of making little holes is why it's a big deal. That is, fire is something that will eventually destroy your heart and decapitate you and a lot more. But they're not &quot;vulnerable&quot; to it anymore than they are &quot;vulnerable&quot; to a sword just because it can decapitate them. I'm digressing. Yeah, fire being such a huge deal in this game has always been an odd thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:25:37-07:00","id":1208575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1208548-so-is-armor-in-mage-an-auto-soak-or-dice?p=1208569#post1208569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I'm iffy about fire even in the case of vampires. Many versions of vampires aren't &quot;vulnerable&quot; to fire per se. They just aren't particularly invulnerable to it, and the fact that it eventually destroys something utterly instead of making little holes is why it's a big deal. That is, fire is something that will eventually destroy your heart and decapitate you and a lot more. But they're not &quot;vulnerable&quot; to it anymore than they are &quot;vulnerable&quot; to a sword just because it can decapitate them. I'm digressing. Yeah, fire being such a huge deal in this game has always been an odd thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean in the Mage lore fire is the &quot;force of undoing&quot; or something which destroys patterns.<br /> <br /> However:<br /> <br /> - Fire, itself, has a pattern.<br /> <br /> - Fire doesn't unravel all patterns. It burns things which are flammable.<br /> <br /> - The idea that fire is a consuming force which undoes ordered structures and reduces them into something else is pretty niche in a metaphysical world where reality is anyone's game. Fire being a &quot;force of undoing&quot; which naturally does Aggravated damage would make sense in the Dark Ages perhaps, but in most paradigms fire is just, well, fire. And if your paradigm has Aggravated Fire, you can awaken the Spirit within the Fire or use Prime to raise it up to a greater form which matches up to your theory. The only way Fire could exist as it does in M20 would be if Fire doing Aggravated was one of the Earthly Foundations, which seems like a stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T00:39:08-07:00","id":1208753,"title":"","content":"Fire also holds the metaphysical force of purification and consuming corruption, which is a major factor why vampires fear it that much. It's not about the mages paradigm in this case, it's about what vampires believe they are. Also, the fact alone that vampires can not deal with fire any more than mortals makes it such a good weapon against blood suckers (this is the same reason why shotguns are so useful against vampires, too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T07:29:23-07:00","id":1208852,"title":"","content":"Damn vampires, forcing everyone to suffer Agg from fire just because they believe they're uncleand and corrupt and that fire should purify them :P . But really, fire shouldn't do Agg damage to anything that ain't suffering from a biblical curse.<br /> <br /> But going back to the thread: No, in Mage armors can't &quot;auto soak&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, to reduce the damage of an attack that way with a forcefield or similar magick, substracting damage successes from the attack (as a sort of &quot;auto-soak armor&quot;) it's not unheard off. It's a bit of a gray area, though (books are contradictory about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}